    {
      "heading": "Skill loss",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Upon Death, if the player is not under the effect of no skill drain as granted by another recent death, the player loses a portion of each skill level according to configured World Modifiers (default: 5%) and also loses all progress towards the next skill level."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Note",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "In fact, the skill level is a floating number with an integer part and a decimal part. The integer part is used for all purposes: displayed in the UI, used to determine the strength of the skill effects and the experience needed for the next level. The decimal part is not linked to the progression toward the next level, its only effect is to sometime save a level on death. Examples:\n• A player with a skill at level 50 dies: the new skill level is 50 × ( 1 − 0.05 ) = 47.5 {\\textstyle 50\\times (1-0.05)=47.5} effectively 47 for all purposes.\n• If this player dies again at 47.5 (effectively 47): the new skill level is 47.5 × ( 1 − 0.05 ) = 45.125 {\\textstyle 47.5\\times (1-0.05)=45.125} , effectively 45.\n• Whereas if a player is at 47.0 (also effectively 47): the new skill level is 47.0 × ( 1 − 0.05 ) = 44.65 {\\textstyle 47.0\\times (1-0.05)=44.65} , effectively 44.\n• Gaining a level doesn't round the level it just add +1 to the current value, the next level after 47.5 is 48.5, etc.\nNote that progress to the next level does not factor into this calculation."
    }
